# Optional, server-side only. Without a key, live Ethereum history uses Blockscout's
# keyless public explorer; the synthetic test fixture stays offline either way.
# Supply your own existing permitted Etherscan API key locally; never commit it.
# With a key, Etherscan serves Ethereum and Arbitrum One. It returns ETH and ERC-20
# transfers but not internal ones, which only Blockscout supplies. Derive Chain always
# uses its own keyless Blockscout explorer, since Etherscan has no Derive history.
# Also enables prices read at each transfer's own block: those come from Uniswap
# swap logs, and the public RPC refuses the archive requests they would otherwise
# need. Without it, USD falls back to today's spot price and says so.
ETHERSCAN_API_KEY=

# Keyless live history sends each traced wallet to eth.blockscout.com, and Derive Chain
# expansions to explorer.derive.xyz. Set to off to keep wallets away from both; Ethereum
# history then needs the key above and Derive history is unavailable. Empty or on keeps it.
FLOWLENS_BLOCKSCOUT=

# No Arkham client is enabled. A key alone does not establish integration rights.
